  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Competition Reforms for Enhanced Welfare (CREW)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&#x2022;	To develop better tools that governments, business and consumer groups  can  use to  capture the benefits that accrue to poor consumers and entrepreneurs from greater market competition in priority DFID countries in African and Asian markets. Key stakeholders will use these tools to push for competition reforms in at least 3 DFID countries (Zambia, Ghana and India) that will reduce prices of certain goods and/or services for all poor consumers and entrepreneurs by the end of 2016. This contributes  towards our MDGs by increasing poor peoples&#x2019; ability to buy more goods and services thus enhancing their well- being.</narrative>
  </description>
